  "closure": "Full author mathematical body151–1340 retained. Exact Theorem2 statement201–203 and full primary959–1009 are preserved, with the complete newly necessary mass-loss Proposition3 statement232–244 and full supporting Section3 proof576–953. Its recursive decomposition, pointed independence and region-size estimates, including required new native core499–568, are retained along with the precise tree/excursion setup269–343 and decomposition definitions. Classical Aldous decomposition and Brownian excursion regularity/maximum distribution remain exact author references. The final symmetry argument applies the source result separately to the inverse map, without introducing a bi-Holder assumption. Original native figure selection is bound to exact observed PDF Forms; numerical exponent discussion, discrete subtree estimates and the existence appendix are unselected claims.",
  "current_difficulty_reason": "A homeomorphism can align branch points adaptively, so mismatch at one random branch or a fixed map does not give a simultaneous obstruction for all homeomorphisms. The authors control exponentially many admissible branch-point chains and use a corrected positive-martingale mismatch argument to force uniform loss of region mass across recursive scales. Only after that new probabilistic core do Brownian excursion regularity and region-diameter bounds convert the mass loss into the strict Holder obstruction.",
  "editorial_changes": [
    "Independent article layout and explicit source, scope and difficulty boundary",
    "Bibliography restored from exact matching cached publisher HTML with native math annotations",
    "Necessary native macro definitions retained; only publisher typography commands mapped to ordinary article equivalents"
